@startuml remote-worker-turn
' Revision 2026-10-12: R-WORKPLACE service controls, helper-v1 activation and execution-level stops; Draft, no renderer/qualification evidence.
title Remote worker turn (revision 6; B boundary shown, disabled until separate provisioner spec/qualification): the harness has no local tools; the relay (harness identity) forwards to the bridge service (bridge identity), which carries every tool call and the mailbox over ONE SSH connection from the donor to our host; our host never connects back

box "Donor machine: harness identity (sandboxed, egress = proxy only)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Harness\n(Claude / Codex / Muse, lockdown plan)" as H
  participant "swarma-remote-tools\n(stdio relay; no keys, no network)" as MCP
  participant "Provider proxy" as PX
end box
box "Donor machine: bridge identity (keys, audit, cursors)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Bridge service\n(supervisor + SSH client + signer + admission)" as SUP
end box
box "Our host" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "sshd root + relay-only fixed shell\nswarma-rb-exec (service principal; peer UID/generation)" as RB
  participant "Workplace control state\nservice-owned policy/claims/floors/audit" as WP
  participant "Dispatcher + root launcher/helper\nstart receipt + journaled exec.stop" as D
  participant "Untrusted jobs or runner\nworkplace UID; backend shape unpublished" as JOB
  participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox, M3)" as BR
end box
participant "Orchestrator" as O

note over H, SUP
  The role split is enforced by UID/sandbox in B; sandbox only in C; A shares the donor UID,
  has no OS isolation/egress guarantee, and relies on qualified lockdown with no local tools.
  Relay has no keys/network in every variant; protocol/backend closed formats are pending.
end note

== standing connection ==
SUP -> RB: ssh workplace-user@host with K_ssh + short user-CA certificate;\nhost certificate checked on EVERY connection: pinned host CA, host name, validity, KRL (no TOFU)
note over SUP, RB: Bridge requests renewal; service authenticates workplace; keeper-held CA signs only its principal; expiry/revocation refuses; retire stops renewal and closes sessions.
break failed host trust / expired or revoked user certificate / wrong workplace principal
  SUP -> SUP: refuse connection; no TOFU or alternate trust source
end
RB -> WP: reconcile durable claims and admission floors before opening admission
break missing / restored / unreadable / contradictory claim or floor evidence
  RB -> RB: keep binding admission closed
end
RB --> SUP: hello {versions:[1]} / swarma-rb/1 channel open (bounded CBOR frames, flow credits)
SUP -> RB: policy.get
RB --> SUP: workplace policy {tools, write scope, network, limits, env_allow} -> effective tool set
note right of RB: Match block: root-controlled TrustedUserCAKeys + KRL + workplace principal, no forwarding, no PTY,\nno user rc/env; relay-only fixed shell/forced command by absolute path; no user startup files; reconnect is the donor side's job

== launch ==
SUP -> SUP: obtain the composed plan from the construction site (agents-management);\ncheck expect_pin, tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto, policy generation, qualified tuple;\nvalidate the expanded launch against the generated policy; resolve credential_binding/1
break unqualified/changed/unreadable executable, wrong pin/posture/permissions/generation or credential binding
  SUP -> SUP: refuse before exec; no alternate harness/source
end
SUP -> H: consume composed plan, launch exact qualified build;\nB: harness UID + sandbox + per-UID egress; C: donor UID + sandbox;\nA: donor UID, no OS confinement, direct provider path; credential per launch (CIP-0010)
H -> MCP: MCP initialize; tools/list = effective set (policy intersection)

== task arrives ==
O -> BR: signed task message to the worker (snapshot of one element)
BR -> BR: verify signature, grant, decision guard, fence; mailbox record; cursor++
BR -> RB: mailbox.notify {message_id, cursor} (advisory)
RB -> SUP: frame mailbox.notify
SUP -> RB: mailbox.read {from_cursor}
RB -> BR: read
BR --> RB: items + verification records
RB --> SUP: frames
SUP -> SUP: DONOR-SIDE ADMISSION: verification record present, target binding = this worker,\nunexpired, not fenced/revoked, delivery mode allowed; dedup by message_id; persist; cursor++
break absent/invalid verification, wrong binding, expired/fenced/revoked item or disallowed delivery mode
  SUP -> SUP: refuse input; do not apply a turn
end
SUP -> H: next turn through the session-input adapter: "validated message <id>" + snapshot
SUP -> RB: mailbox.applied {message_id} (application receipt, distinct from the transport reply)

== work ==
loop each tool call
  H -> MCP: tools/call bash {cmd, cwd, timeout}
  MCP -> SUP: forward over the relay socket (peer credentials checked)
  SUP -> SUP: audit line {tool, args_sha256, bytes, at}; budget counters (trusted side)
  break tool outside effective policy or wrong local peer
    SUP --> MCP: error result; audit refusal
    MCP --> H: unavailable tool
  end
  SUP -> RB: frame exec {id, op_key, cmd, cwd, env (env_allow only), timeout_s <= policy, max_output_bytes <= policy, lease_s}
  RB -> WP: authenticate new-versus-retry admission; binding-generation identity, operation, argument digest
  break operation/argument mismatch or unseen expired identity below sequence/epoch floor
    WP --> RB: refuse without mutation (exact codes unpublished)
    RB --> SUP: refusal
  end
  alt existing durable claim
    WP -> WP: reconcile/observe same effect; never automatically re-execute
    WP --> RB: retained recorded result or pending / unknown_result
  else genuinely new operation admitted in current bounded window
    WP -> WP: durably claim identity + operation + canonical-argument digest BEFORE mutation
    WP -> D: authorized execution via existing launcher/receipt path; caps and lease service-owned
    D -> JOB: start under workplace UID; admitted shape/concurrency unpublished
    JOB --> WP: output and result evidence
    WP -> WP: persist result + service audit outside workplace UID
    WP --> RB: stdout/stderr frames (seq), exit
  end
  RB --> SUP: frames (output cached separately for 10 min; cache miss never authorizes mutation)
  SUP --> MCP: result
  MCP --> H: tool result
end
H -> PX: B/C: model API calls through the qualified proxy only
alt the model requests a built-in tool (Bash, Edit, WebFetch ...)
  H -> H: harness returns an error tool result (tool not available);\nthe tripwire logs the name after dispatch and may end the turn
end
alt SSH channel drops mid-turn
  SUP -> SUP: pause the turn loop; running turn continues to its deadline;\ntool calls fail with channel_down (retryable); result post queued durably with its op_key
  SUP -> RB: reconnect with backoff; host certificate/CA/validity/KRL rechecked; catch up from the durable cursor;\nretry keeps original identity/arguments/admission window; reconcile same durable claim;\nretained result or pending / unknown_result, never automatic re-execution
end

== execution cleanup ==
opt lease expires / cancel / channel loss after grace
  RB -> D: journaled execution stop under existing effect ID
  D -> JOB: exec.stop under published scope; signal and verify same execution process set
  break absence unknown / contradictory / unavailable
    D --> RB: retain affected claims; block replay/restart; no process-group-only proof
  end
  D --> RB: confirmed execution absence
end
note over D, JOB
  Serialized per-job execution or standing runner shape remains unpublished.
  Runner per-job cancel is best effort; unknown descendants stop whole runner execution,
  retaining all affected job claims as unknown; restart requires prior absence + fresh admission.
end note

== result ==
H -> MCP: tools/call mailbox_post {binding, text} (offered only when the policy grants it)
MCP -> SUP: forward
SUP -> SUP: build the FINAL envelope (canonical bytes; audience/thread from the task record);\nsign with K_sig (D0 variant-specific storage; never sent to the project)
SUP -> RB: frame mailbox.post {op_key, envelope_bytes, signature}; original admission window on retry
RB -> WP: authenticate admission; durable binding-generation identity/argument claim before effect
break conflicting arguments / expired new admission / unresolved existing claim
  WP --> SUP: refuse or pending / unknown_result; no automatic post
end
alt existing conclusive remote post claim
  WP --> RB: retained result or unknown_result if output unavailable; no second post
  RB --> SUP: same-effect outcome
else genuinely new post admitted and claimed before effect
  WP -> BR: verify K_sig signature, grant, freshness; durable mailbox admission claim
  BR -> O: carry final bytes UNCHANGED under project carrier authority (first slice, audited) -> outcome proposal
end
note over H, O
  Phase: Draft donor target after slice 0 + project helper v1/workplace qualification; A first, B disabled, C qualified fallback.
  B proxy identity is bridge UID or a system service; A provider path is direct, no proxy.
  Bridge-role supervisor owns audit/budgets/cursors/dedup and durable queued results;
  harness role owns home/scratch; project bridge owns mailbox and project carrier credential;
  service-principal executor owns policy/caps, execution leases, durable identity/digest claims and admission floors; root sshd owns CA/KRL/relay shell; project keeper/hardware token holds user CA private key.
  Workplace activation requires helper v1 fw.apply + applied state including loopback, even A/read-only.
  Write scope = workplace UID writable set; network mode = enforced per-UID firewall.
  Claims discarded only after identities are permanently inadmissible; persist floor first.
  R-OBS where applicable: recorded (result/current state), pending, rolled_back,
  not_recorded (authoritative), unavailable (missing/expired/unreadable), contradictory.
  Original caller/operators observe under receiver journal serialization; absence never retries.
  Ten-minute output retention is independent of claim retention; no new service.
  Exact service-account deployment for project bridge/executor, filenames and claim/floor/cache encoding
  unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D5. rb/1 and workplace-exec/1 are pending design shorthand.
  [[../CIP-0008-remote-worker-launch-mode.md#recommendation CIP-0008 R3/R5/R9]]
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D5/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#tools-mailbox-and-lifecycle Delivery and reconnect]]
end note

@enduml
